# Implementation Plan: Delegation & Substitute Approval System

This plan outlines the steps to implement a centralized delegation system where Admins can manage approver absences and assign substitutes, automating the routing logic for leave requests.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **CEO Role Mapping**: This implementation assumes the `ADMINISTRATOR` role in the system represents the CEO.
> **PDF Generation**: The "Approval Scenarios" documentation will be generated as a high-fidelity PDF using the existing corporate branding assets.

## Proposed Changes

### 1. Database Schema

#### [MODIFY] [schema.prisma](file:///c:/Apps/Leave%20Tracker/server/prisma/schema.prisma)
- Add `substituteId` (String?) to the `User` model.
- Add a self-relation for delegation.
- Add `isAway` (Boolean) if not already fully utilized.

### 2. Backend Logic

#### [MODIFY] [approvalUtils.ts](file:///c:/Apps/Leave%20Tracker/server/src/utils/approvalUtils.ts)
- Create a centralized `getEffectiveApprover(role: string)` function.
- This function will check if the primary role holder is `isAway` and return the `substitute` if available.
- Implement `isCEOAway()` specific check.

#### [MODIFY] [leave.controller.ts](file:///c:/Apps/Leave%20Tracker/server/src/controllers/leave.controller.ts)
- **Routing**: Update `createLeaveRequest` to check if the initial line manager is away and notify the substitute instead.
- **Auto-Approval**: Update `gmApproveLeaveRequest` to check `isCEOAway()`. If true, set status directly to `APPROVED`.
- **Double-Approval**: If a substitute approves and they are also the next level approver, automatically process both levels.
- **Notifications**: Add logic to notify the "Expected Approver" when an action is taken on their behalf (Rule 6).

#### [NEW] [delegation.controller.ts](file:///c:/Apps/Leave%20Tracker/server/src/controllers/delegation.controller.ts)
- Create endpoints for Admins to:
    - List all approvers and their current status.
    - Toggle `isAway` for any user.
    - Assign/Update a `substituteId` for any user.

### 3. Frontend Implementation

#### [NEW] [DelegationManagement.tsx](file:///c:/Apps/Leave%20Tracker/src/pages/Admin/DelegationManagement.tsx)
- A "World Class" UI for Admins to manage the delegation matrix.
- Vibrant status indicators for "Active" vs "Absent" managers.
- Searchable user selection for assigning substitutes.

#### [MODIFY] [corporatePdf.ts](file:///c:/Apps/Leave%20Tracker/src/lib/corporatePdf.ts)
- Update PDF templates to show "Approved by [Substitute] on behalf of [Original Approver]" when applicable.

### 4. Documentation PDF

#### [NEW] [generate-scenarios-pdf.ts](file:///c:/Apps/Leave%20Tracker/server/src/scripts/generate-scenarios-pdf.ts)
- A script to generate a beautifully branded PDF document detailing the 5 scenarios listed in our discussion.
- This will use the same high-fidelity styling as the official leave forms.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- Scripted tests to verify:
    - Request routing to substitute when manager is away.
    - CEO bypass when `isAway` is true for Admin.
    - Correct notification triggers for substitutes and absentees.

### Manual Verification
1. Login as Admin.
2. Mark OM as "Absent" and GM as "Substitute".
3. Submit a leave as an Operations employee.
4. Verify GM receives the notification and can approve.
5. Verify PDF shows delegation details.
